* Diode-connected devices fed by a resistor from the rail
* The smallest circuit whose operating point is an intersection of a
* resistive load line with the device's own surface, rather than a current
* the deck imposes. Every other diode-connected device in this catalog
* (current_mirror, cascode_stack, self_biased_cascode) is fed by an ideal
* current source, which pins the current and leaves only the voltage to
* solve; here both are the model's to find.
<MODEL_SETUP>
Vdd vdd 0 <VDD>
Vbn bn 0 <BODY_N>
Vbp bp 0 <BODY_P>
Rn vdd nr <DIODE_RLOAD>
<N_PREFIX>n_dio nr nr 0 bn <N_DEVICE>
Rp np 0 <DIODE_RLOAD>
<P_PREFIX>p_dio np np vdd bp <P_DEVICE>
<OUTPUT_LOAD>
.temp <TEMP>
<ANALYSIS>
.end
